  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Sean Cairncross said he was extremely interested in ways to build U.S. open source AI, make it competitive, and make it the preferential adoption by the world. He described balancing the innovation side of running at speed with securing systems and handling the technology responsibly, and said technical security should not be seen as a barrier to innovation. He characterized an executive order as designed to be non-regulatory while putting in place a system to work with industry, and noted a tendency for government to want to adjust the dials directly.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s3",
    "s5",
    "s7",
    "s6"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Sean Cairncross said he was extremely interested in ways to build U.S. open source AI, make it competitive, and make it the preferential adoption by the world.",
